  "final_report": "[stop_reason: hop_cap_reached | hops used: 4/4]\n\nAnalyst summary:\n**Investigation focus \u2013\u202fPotential supply\u2011chain fallout from a disruption at Gazprom (identified by the 2022\u201109\u201102 event date).**\n\n| Company that appears to be affected | What the filings say (evidence) | How many independent sources |\n|-------------------------------------|---------------------------------|------------------------------|\n| **Eni S.p.A.** | \u2022\u202fIn several 2009\u20112010 SEC\u2011style filings Eni reports that Gazprom *exercised a call option* to buy back the 20\u202f% stake Eni held in OAO\u202fGazprom\u202fNeft (April\u202f7\u202f2009) and later a 51\u202f% interest in the joint venture OOO\u202fSeverEnergia. The cash consideration was recorded (\u2248\u202fUS$4.2\u202fbn). <br>\u2022\u202fEni also notes that, as part of agreements with Gazprom, its **off\u2011take of Russian gas for the Italian market fell by 0.97\u202fBCM** (2008) and later **by 2.75\u202fBCM in 2009**, reflecting Gazprom\u2019s entry into the supply market for Italian importers.<br>\u2022\u202fA 2012 filing records a *pre\u2011liminary agreement* with Gazprom to revise long\u2011term Russian\u2011gas supply contracts, retroactive to early\u20112011. <br>These points are taken from three separate Eni filings (2009\u201104\u201107, 2009\u201104\u201124, 2010\u201104\u201126 and 2012\u201104\u201105). | **Two** \u2013 the same company\u2019s own filing (get_supplier_info not called) plus a corpus\u2011wide search that returned multiple Eni documents. |\n| **Shell plc** | \u2022\u202fA 2022 filing lists Shell\u2019s *joint\u2011venture stakes* with Gazprom\u2011related entities (Sakhalin\u20112, Salym Petroleum Development N.V., Gydan joint venture) and its participation in the **Nord\u202fStream\u202f2** financing project. The filing states that \u201cdecisions to exit ventures with Gazprom\u2026 will impact the carrying value of the related assets and lead to impairments in 2022.\u201d <br>\u2022\u202fThe same document also notes Shell\n\nCOVERAGE GAPS (26) -- reported explicitly, not omitted:\n  - saudi arabian oil: no evidence gathered\n  - united co rusal international pjsc: no evidence gathered\n  - cpc corp/taiwan: no evidence gathered\n  - chevron: no evidence gathered\n  - jordan petroleum refinery: no evidence gathered\n  - sk: no evidence gathered\n  - hyundai engineering & construction: no evidence gathered\n  - bp: no evidence gathered\n  - hyundai motor: no evidence gathered\n  - e1: no evidence gathered\n  - nippon steel: no evidence gathered\n  - tenaris: no evidence gathered\n  - korea electric power: no evidence gathered\n  - sk innovation: no evidence gathered\n  - alcoa: no evidence gathered\n  - mitsui: no evidence gathered\n  - apple: no evidence gathered\n  - saudi basic industries: no evidence gathered\n  - formosa petrochemical: no evidence gathered\n  - triangle tyre: no evidence gathered\n  - formosa chemicals & fibre: no evidence gathered\n  - glencore: no evidence gathered\n  - arcelormittal: no evidence gathered\n  - posco: no evidence gathered\n  - posco eco & challenge: no evidence gathered\n  - s-oil: no evidence gathered",
